<section>
  <h4>Features</h4>
  <p>WordPress site monitoring with GCM and MetaManager status.</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Real-time status checking every 60 seconds</li>
    <li>Browser notifications on status changes</li>
    <li>GCM server status (uptime, disk, memory, SSL)</li>
    <li>MetaManager daemon status (queues, tools)</li>
    <li>JSON export and import</li>
    <li>Data stored in localStorage — no server required</li>
  </ul>
</section>
<section>
  <h4>How It Works</h4>
  <p>The app fetches status from your WordPress REST API endpoints using Application Passwords for authentication.</p>
  <p><strong>GCM:</strong> <code>/wp-json/gcm/v1/status</code></p>
  <p><strong>MetaManager:</strong> <code>/wp-json/metamanager/v1/status</code></p>
  <p>All data is stored in your browser's localStorage. Nothing is sent to any external service.</p>
</section>
<section>
  <h4>Setup</h4>
  <p>For each WordPress site, create an Application Password in Users > Profile > Application Passwords. Enter the site URL, your username, and the generated password.</p>
</section>
